hings to say"). The third speaker responds by saying they are "Almost" done, but "first we got to start." This juxtaposition sarcastically points out that despite the first speaker running out of words, the actual process or task has not yet begun, indicating no progress has been made toward the goal.\n\nAnswer: \boxed{D}
