c accompaniment rather than a distinct, independent melody playing against the main melody (which isn't clearly established as separate from the chords here).\n\nThe rhythmic disruption caused by the syncopated chords strongly suggests they are contributing to the overall feeling of **harmonic tension and release** by driving the groove forward and creating rhythmic anticipation.\n\nAnswer: $\boxed{B}$
